  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(i^2=-1,\\) then the sum \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\cos45^\\circ+i\\cos135^\\circ+\\cdots\\\\ &\\quad+i^n\\cos(45+90n)^\\circ+\\cdots\\\\ &\\quad+i^{40}\\cos3645^\\circ \\end{aligned} \\] equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-10i\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{21\\sqrt2}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}(21-20i)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}(21+20i)\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1977-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(u_n=i^n\\cos(45+90n)^\\circ.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} u_{n+2} &=i^{n+2}\\cos(225+90n)^\\circ\\\\ &=(-i^n)(-\\cos(45+90n)^\\circ)\\\\ &=u_n. \\end{aligned} \\] Every even-indexed term equals \\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2},\\) and every odd-indexed term equals \\(-\\frac{i\\sqrt2}{2}.\\) There are \\(21\\) even indices and \\(20\\) odd indices, so the sum is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}(21-20i).\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare the term indexed by \\(n+2\\) with the term indexed by \\(n\\)",
        "Count the even and odd indices from \\(0\\) through \\(40\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
